{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Come, let us deal wisely with him.</b> On his account." "<b>And it shall be, when war befalls.</b> An expression of occurrence and chance event, like ותקראנה אותי כאלה. And we find a plural form used for a singular in connection with war: וכי תבואו מלחמה בארצכם. And in another place it says: ידה ליתד תשלחנה. The meaning: when the wars of enemies befall. Another interpretation: it is an abbreviated form, as if it were written: כי תקראנה קורות מלחמה. And similar to it: וברוב יועצים תקום, since it is as if it were written וברך ברכה, and לא אשיבנה." "<b>And he will also join himself to our enemies.</b> Like one whose curse hangs upon his fellow. Another interpretation: he will join with our enemies, and by means of that, <b>and go up from the land</b> against our will."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The final phrase לא אשיבנה is puzzling in context; translated hyper-literally. The connection of the וברך ברכה example to abbreviation is itself unclear."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:42.122917595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}